<h2>Media</h2>
<h3>Hasil Cetakan</h3>
Media.
Hasil Cetakan.
SSatoshi Hase membuat serial novel, dengan ilustrasi oleh anggota Supercell member Redjuice, di majalah Newtype Kadokawa Shoten dari tahun 2011 hingga 2012. Novel ini disusun dan diterbitkan dalam bentuk buku pada 10 Oktober 2012 (). Pada tahun 2013, Tokyo Otaku Mode mulai menyelenggarakan terjemahan bahasa Inggris dari novel tersebut, dengan versi animasi ilustrasi Redjuice yang dikerjakan Wit Studio dan animator Satoshi Kadowaki. Selama panel mereka di Anime Expo 2019, J-Novel Club mengumumkan kemitraan dengan Tokyo Otaku Mode untuk merilis novel di Amerika Utara.
The novel has inspired three separate manga series. Kagura Uguisu published the two-volume manga series Beatless: Dystopia in Kadokawa's shōnen manga magazine Monthly Shōnen Ace between 2012 and 2013. A single-volume four-panel spin-off manga, titled Beatless, was published by Kila. , a spin-off manga series written by Gun Snark and illustrated by Mitsuru Ohsaki, was launched on Kadokawa's Famitsu Comic Clear website on April 11, 2014, with a preview chapter having been published on March 14. It has been compiled into eight volumes.
<h3>Anime</h3>
Anime.
A 24-episode anime television series adaptation aired from January 13 to September 28, 2018. Episodes 21-24 are also referred to as Beatless: Final Stage. The series is directed by Seiji Mizushima at Diomedéa and written by Tatsuya Takahashi and Gō Zappa, with character designs by Hiroko Yaguchi. The first opening theme is "Error" by Garnidelia and the first ending theme is "Primalove" by ClariS. The second opening theme is "Truth." by TrySail, and the second ending theme is "Shapeless" by Tokyo Performance Doll. The series is streaming exclusively on Amazon Video worldwide.
